## Feature summary (web, SideFX reference)

- Source: https://www.sidefx.com/docs/houdini/nodes/cop/grunge_layerednoise.html
- Summary (EN): Grunge Layered Noise layers several simple noise patterns, built from Fractal Noise COPs, into a default pattern that looks like a stormy sky reflected in water. It works as a building block for intricate textures, such as smoky skies.
- Résumé (FR) : Grunge Layered Noise superpose quatre couches de bruit pour imiter un ciel d'orage reflété dans l'eau, brique utile pour des fumées.

- Inputs meaning: ["size_ref: sets only the output image size and metadata, not the pattern"]

- Key parameters: ["Range: Amplitude and Center set the output from C-A to C+A; Mask Contrast increases extremes before them", "Pattern: Element Size, Element Scale (with Per-Component Controls), Offset, Tile Size", "Base Noise: web-shaped starting pattern, with Amplitude and Element Size", "Base Cells: carves cellular boundaries into the base noise, with Amplitude, Element Size and Complement", "Secondary Noise: fine detail in darker areas, with Amplitude, Center, Element Size and Complement", "Secondary Cells: final cellular layer, most visible in the brightest and darkest areas, with Amplitude, Center, Element Size and Complement", "Post Processing, applied in order: Fold, Complement, Bias, Gain, Gamma, Contrast, Clamp Minimum, Clamp Maximum"]

- Caveats: ["Layers can hold negative values and values above 1; use the Clamp options", "Complement and Bias-style operations assume values from 0 to 1", "Fold has no visible effect when all values are positive", "Post-processing Contrast differs from Noise Contrast on some noise nodes"]

